    <header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>Kirk Sweeney</h1></header>
    <p>Hi, I'm Kirk. I build data platforms and data solutions for a living. I have built these across leading cloud platforms and worked with technologies such as Spark, Databricks, Kafka, Pulsar, Kubernetes, Apache Beam, and more.</p>
    <p>I love to learn new things, and I created this blog as a place to share some of my learnings. Feel free to ask questions below each blog post, or send a message via <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kirk-sweeney/">LinkedIn</a>.</p>
    <h2>Topics covered</h2>
    <ul><li>Data platform paradigms: lakehouses, data mesh, and related approaches</li><li>Data engineering: SQL, Spark, Flink, and more</li><li>Software development: Python, Java, Rust, and more</li><li>DevOps workflows: Kubernetes, CI/CD, Terraform, Argo CD, and more</li></ul>
    <h2>Working principles</h2>
    <ul><li>We must be customer- and people-obsessed.</li><li>To understand our customers' problems, we must work closely with them.</li><li>Investing in tooling is necessary to continuously release working software.</li><li>We should minimize processes that slow our response to change.</li><li>The best teams are built on trust, both within the team and from management.</li></ul>
